{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nMr. Chanek has an integer represented by a string $$$s$$$. Zero or more digits have been erased and are denoted by the character _. There are also zero or more digits marked by the character X, meaning they're the same digit.Mr. Chanek wants to count the number of possible integer $$$s$$$, where $$$s$$$ is divisible by $$$25$$$. Of course, $$$s$$$ must not contain any leading zero. He can replace the character _ with any digit. He can also replace the character X with any digit, but it must be the same for every character X.As a note, a leading zero is any 0 digit that comes before the first nonzero digit in a number string in positional notation. For example, 0025 has two leading zeroes. An exception is the integer zero, (0 has no leading zero, but 0000 has three leading zeroes).\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n\n    private static int[][][] cache;\n\n    public static int compute(int idx, int fixedDigit, int prevTwo, String s) {\n        if (idx == s.length()) {\n            return (prevTwo == 0 || prevTwo == 25 || prevTwo == 50 || prevTwo == 75) ? 1 : 0;\n        }\n        if (cache[idx][fixedDigit][prevTwo] != -1) {\n            return cache[idx][fixedDigit][prevTwo];\n        }\n        int res = 0;\n        char ch = s.charAt(idx);\n        if (ch == 'X') {\n            if (fixedDigit != 10) {\n                res = compute(idx + 1, fixedDigit, (prevTwo % 10) * 10 + fixedDigit, s);\n            } else {\n                for (int d = (idx == 0 ? 1 : 0); d < 10; d++) {\n                    res += compute(idx + 1, d, (prevTwo % 10) * 10 + d, s);\n                }\n            }\n        } else if (ch == '_') {\n            for (int d = (idx == 0 ? 1 : 0); d < 10; d++) {\n                res += compute(idx + 1, fixedDigit, (prevTwo % 10) * 10 + d, s);\n            }\n        } else {\n            int digit = ch - '0';\n            res += compute(idx + 1, fixedDigit, (prevTwo % 10) * 10 + digit, s);\n        }\n        cache[idx][fixedDigit][prevTwo] = res;\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String input = br.readLine();\n        int n = input.length();\n        if (n == 1) {\n            System.out.println(input.equals(\"0\") ? 1 : 0);\n        } else if (input.charAt(0) == '0') {\n            System.out.println(0);\n        } else {\n            cache = new int[n][11][100];\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                for (int j = 0; j < 11; j++) {\n                    Arrays.fill(cache[i][j], -1);\n                }\n            }\n            System.out.println(compute(0, 10, 0, input));\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n\n    private static int[][][] cache;\n    private static String s;\n    private static int n;\n\n    public static int compute(int idx, int fixedDigit, int prevTwo) {\n        if (idx == n) {\n            return (prevTwo == 0 || prevTwo == 25 || prevTwo == 50 || prevTwo == 75) ? 1 : 0;\n        }\n        if (cache[idx][fixedDigit][prevTwo] != -1) {\n            return cache[idx][fixedDigit][prevTwo];\n        }\n        int res = 0;\n        char ch = s.charAt(idx);\n        if (ch == 'X') {\n            if (fixedDigit != 10) {\n                // X has been assigned a digit, use it\n                int newPrevTwo = (prevTwo % 10) * 10 + fixedDigit;\n                res = compute(idx + 1, fixedDigit, newPrevTwo);\n            } else {\n                // X hasn't been assigned yet, try all digits 0-9\n                for (int d = 0; d < 10; d++) {\n                    // Check leading zero constraint\n                    if (idx == 0 && d == 0) continue;\n                    int newPrevTwo = (prevTwo % 10) * 10 + d;\n                    res += compute(idx + 1, d, newPrevTwo);\n                }\n            }\n        } else if (ch == '_') {\n            for (int d = (idx == 0 ? 1 : 0); d < 10; d++) {\n                int newPrevTwo = (prevTwo % 10) * 10 + d;\n                res += compute(idx + 1, fixedDigit, newPrevTwo);\n            }\n        } else {\n            int digit = ch - '0';\n            // Check for leading zero\n            if (idx == 0 && digit == 0) {\n                res = 0;\n            } else {\n                int newPrevTwo = (prevTwo % 10) * 10 + digit;\n                res = compute(idx + 1, fixedDigit, newPrevTwo);\n            }\n        }\n        cache[idx][fixedDigit][prevTwo] = res;\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        s = br.readLine();\n        n = s.length();\n        \n        // Special case: single character\n        if (n == 1) {\n            if (s.equals(\"0\") || s.equals(\"_\") || s.equals(\"X\")) {\n                System.out.println(1);\n            } else {\n                System.out.println(0);\n            }\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        // Check if first character is fixed zero\n        if (s.charAt(0) != '_' && s.charAt(0) != 'X' && s.charAt(0) == '0') {\n            System.out.println(0);\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        cache = new int[n][11][100];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < 11; j++) {\n                Arrays.fill(cache[i][j], -1);\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(compute(0, 10, 0));\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.116541382856667e-05, -2.7418097943154862e-06, 0.0, -1.3351351299206726e-05, -2.3483953555114567e-05, -2.50339189733495e-06, -7.271740287251305e-06, -2.8132995794294402e-05, -1.5616295058862306e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.753696753643453e-05, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.6331539882230572e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00769093818962574, -4.529942543740617e-06, -0.7278206944465637, -2.2411095415009186e-05, -0.6334112882614136, -0.0001760566228767857, -0.4287036061286926, -0.008616176433861256, -9.202533692587167e-05, -4.529942543740617e-06, -0.10500398278236389, -0.0013677061069756746, -0.2255474478006363, -0.026305440813302994, -7.390948667307384e-06, -5.006777428206988e-06, -0.04381490871310234, -0.0008188708452507854, -0.0008048156159929931, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.003197915619239211, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.02326641045510769, -4.565611743601039e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -3.099436753473128e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.17978927493095398, -0.005695424973964691, -0.0069976020604372025, -8.141662692651153e-05, -0.0003084660565946251, -0.010867222212255001, -0.00019691436318680644, -0.142695039